  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. The project has expanded its team with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, including an onboarding session on September 10th. Key developments include a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, a partnership with TechInnovate for AI research, and a move into the development phase led by Omar Jensen. The compliance plan budget has been increased to $55,000. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and a detailed progress report will be presented on November 20th."
